  "rationale": "The representative failure is a noun after the opening determiner “The”: the model strongly favors “End,” whose existing suffix rule also matches this incomplete opening context. The batch also shows proper names after “with” and after a comma receiving very low probability when the captured-person feature does not apply. Add modest evidence for plausible title nouns only when the entire prefix is the single token “The,” and a reusable suffix cue for person-name continuations after “with” or a comma. These are probabilistic cues, not claims that other nouns or continuations are impossible. In particular, the title-noun pairing is supported by few examples and could overfavor these nouns in other bare-determiner contexts; the name cue preserves alternatives among names.",
